※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 3014 LANG_SYNTAX_NOT_ASSOCIATIVE

※ A comparison answers with a truth value, so a second one beside it would be
※ comparing that answer with a number.  Rust refuses the same thing; C and Go
※ give it that meaning and let it be a mistake.
let a: u8 = 1u8
let b: u8 = 2u8
let c: u8 = 3u8

@[startup]
fn main() → bool:
    a < b < c
